lesson chemistry-year-review-2 v=1 format=review grade=2 unit=9 subject=chemistry levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Chemistry review: the second year"
  goal "Look back over the year: solids, liquids and gases, melting, mixing and dissolving, changes, rocks and soil."

  warm-up {
    practice chem.which-state count=1 seed=2 easy-seed=1 hard-seed=1
    practice chem.melt-or-freeze count=1 seed=1 easy-seed=5 hard-seed=2
    practice chem.what-sank count=1 seed=3 easy-seed=1 hard-seed=1
  }
  exercises {
    practice chem.state-clue count=1 seed=2 easy-seed=1 hard-seed=2
    practice chem.solid-or-liquid count=1 seed=4 easy-seed=1 hard-seed=1
    practice chem.dissolve-or-not count=1 seed=2 easy-seed=1 hard-seed=1
    practice chem.cloudy-or-clear count=1 seed=1 easy-seed=1 hard-seed=1
    practice chem.change-undo count=1 seed=5 easy-seed=1 hard-seed=3
    practice chem.rock-fizz count=1 seed=2 easy-seed=1 hard-seed=1
    practice chem.fossil-first count=1 seed=3 easy-seed=1 hard-seed=1
    practice chem.drain-table count=1 seed=2 easy-seed=1 hard-seed=5
    practice chem.quarters-later count=1 seed=1 easy-seed=1 hard-seed=1
  }
  puzzle stars=2 {
    show chem.same-chocolate k=0 r=0 hard-k=1 hard-r=2
  }
  puzzle stars=3 {
    show chem.keep-the-lolly k=1 r=1 easy-k=0 hard-k=2 hard-r=3
  }

  grown-ups """
    This is a check, not a test, to do out on the salt flats before the next year's filtering and
    evaporating begin. The warm-up is the first question of three lessons: a jar of particles to
    name the state of, a change to call melting or freezing, a thing that sank in the water. The
    exercises take one question each from the year: a state from a clue, whether wax is solid at a
    temperature, whether a thing dissolves, which glass is cloudy, whether a change can be undone,
    which rock fizzes, which fossil picture comes first, which soil a number belongs to, and how
    much of the cube is left later. Anything that needs the way in again is worth another week
    with that lesson, and everything else can move on. The two puzzles are there to be enjoyed:
    the chocolate star asks whether it is the same chocolate, and the lolly's place has to be
    cold and out of the sun at once, so ask for the reason as well as the answer.
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level the particles have their moving marks drawn, the change is ice melting, the thing that sank sits beside one that floats, the clue names the state plainly, the temperature is far from the melting point, the things to judge dissolve or plainly do not, the other glass holds sand, the change to undo is melting or freezing, one rock fizzes, the fossil picture is the first or the last, the soil's number is read straight off, the cube is on the table, the chocolate star is the two-star, and the lolly stays at home in the freezer."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the particles have no moving marks, the change is water freezing or chocolate melting, the thing that sank sits beside one that dissolved, the clue is the subtler one, the temperature is near the melting point, the things to judge are flour and iron filings, the other glass holds flour, the change to undo is dissolving or rising dough, two or three rocks fizz, the fossil picture is a middle one, the soil is the one that let most or least through, the cube is in the sun, the two-star is the water frozen and thawed, and the lolly's place has to be shaded and shut."
  }
}
